{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:24741-1","published":"2026-11-11T21:43:26Z","modified":"2026-11-19T17:23:11.988033521Z","related":["CVE-2026-84243","CVE-2026-8674","CVE-2026-86805","CVE-2026-97399"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-84243","CVE-2026-8674","CVE-2026-86805","CVE-2026-97399"],"summary":"Security update for glibc","details":"This update for glibc fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-8674: reachable assert in `resolv/resolv_conf.c:update_from_conf` allows an attacker in a local network to\n  trigger a process crash (bsc#1281297).\n- CVE-2026-84243: directory traversal via `gettext` functions and the `LANGUAGE` environment variable can lead to\n  arbitrary code execution (bsc#1289299).\n- CVE-2026-86805: TOCTOU race condition in the dynamic loader allows local attackers to escalate privileges\n  (bsc#1282509).\n- CVE-2026-97399: one byte out-of-bounds read via function `strncasecmp` on Power8 can lead to a program crash\n  (bsc#1283147).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"glibc","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server 16.1","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/glibc&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Server%2016.1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.40-160100.4.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"glibc":"2.40-160100.4.1","glibc-devel":"2.40-160100.4.1","glibc-devel-static":"2.40-160100.4.1","glibc-extra":"2.40-160100.4.1","glibc-gconv-modules-extra":"2.40-160100.4.1","glibc-html":"2.40-160100.4.1","glibc-i18ndata":"2.40-160100.4.1","glibc-info":"2.40-160100.4.1","glibc-lang":"2.40-160100.4.1","glibc-locale":"2.40-160100.4.1","glibc-locale-base":"2.40-160100.4.1","glibc-profile":"2.40-160100.4.1","glibc-utils":"2.40-160100.4.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:24741-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"glibc","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server for SAP applications 16.1","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/glibc&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Server%20for%20SAP%20applicati